{"base_rate":0.4610303830911493,"brier":0.14133830911492734,"bss":0.4311915226979044,"bss_hi":0.5039582437170479,"bss_lo":0.3506921378980146,"chart":{"base":[659.8,53.3],"fp":[253.6,314.0],"lead":"62,267.7 272,241.4 482,185.3 692,111.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 81% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 78% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 8%; promised 96% → rained 82%"},"rel":"78,431.3 365.2,257.2 667.1,111.4"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08170409511228531,"ess":334.0316097204466,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Essen</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Essen rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>86%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nESSEN-BREDENEY, 6.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 41 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(20&ndash;76) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>226</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>64%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>86%</b></td><td class='num'>230</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Essen</b> <span class=\"muted\">Germany</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>20&ndash;76\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Essen &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Essen\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.06513274336283,377.16814159292034 91.5572602739726,322.16438356164383 176.9260759493671,220.73417721518987 284.75666666666666,109.0 362.1181818181817,41.636363636363626 410.02991304347825,18.0 410.02991304347825,24.330434782608677 362.1181818181817,98.36363636363637 284.75666666666666,184.83333333333334 176.9260759493671,294.4556962025316 91.5572602739726,372.027397260274 59.06513274336283,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"214.18494055482165\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"214.18494055482165\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.06513274336283,369.11504424778764 91.5572602739726,302.2191780821918 176.9260759493671,252.9873417721519 284.75666666666666,154.5 362.1181818181817,122.0 410.02991304347825,70.22608695652173\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 226 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.06513274336283\" cy=\"369.11504424778764\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.5572602739726\" cy=\"302.2191780821918\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"176.9260759493671\" cy=\"252.9873417721519\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 64%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"284.75666666666666\" cy=\"154.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 86%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"362.1181818181817\" cy=\"122.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 86% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 230 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.02991304347825\" cy=\"70.22608695652173\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(46%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Essen the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.55) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.27).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.273</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.347</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.505</td><td class='num'>7.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.551</td><td class='num'>6.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.45657,"lon":7.01228,"n":757,"n_cities":213,"name":"Essen","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003008849557522124,"n":226,"obs":0.035398230088495575,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09479452054794521,"n":73,"obs":0.2191780821917808,"sig":true},{"hi":0.51,"lo":0.2,"mean":0.33594936708860756,"n":79,"obs":0.35443037974683544,"sig":false},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.51,"mean":0.6405555555555557,"n":72,"obs":0.625,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8590909090909088,"n":77,"obs":0.7142857142857143,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9944347826086957,"n":230,"obs":0.8565217391304348,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":6.4,"provisional":false,"rank":41,"rank_hi":76.02499999999998,"rank_lo":19.975,"reliability":0.00977553126436504,"resolution":0.1175164847876971,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"essen","station":"ESSEN-BREDENEY","timezone":"Europe/Berlin"}